nodecode-advisor is a rewrite of ljubomirj's ljubomirj/hermes-advisor-plugin:

  https://github.com/ljubomirj/hermes-advisor-plugin
  commit 37e55975611d38212cf082029ece504f207df656
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Ljubomir Josifovski (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the reviewer's whole instruction (advisor_prompt.py), the tagged
[NIT] / [CONCERN] / [BLOCKER] parsing with the hold-and-reconfirm rule and
the malformed-note filter (models.py), and the review half of runtime.py --
the transcript it builds from a turn, the side call, the WATCHDOG.md
guidance, the one-worker background queue, /advisor's verbs, and the
provider/model override.

Left out, and why: the Hermes-specific surfaces have no Nodecode
counterpart. post_llm_call and on_session_finalize became one :FRAME
observer over the terminal turn facts, so the grace period at shutdown and
the effort to bound hook latency have nothing to bound; ctx.inject_message
became a standing notice under the cell's key, since a cell cannot append a
user message to a session; register_status_segment (the footer badge)
became a line in /advisor's own answer and the notices; the interactive
provider/model picker (ctx.request_model_selection) became the section's
model and provider with /advisor model and /advisor provider for this run;
and the per-session state files became one held-note file per session under
the home. The reviewer itself is now a Nodecode side call (nle:complete),
the same seam the organism uses for side work, so no HTTP, credentials or
client of its own are carried.
